{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to DeleteMe for their support of PBS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3200,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the most important reasons we go to space \nis to know our own planet better. Today I'm going  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8560,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tell you about an orbiting facility \nthat literally watches Earth's biosphere  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "breath and grow and die with incredible \nresolution. I'll talk about its profound  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20160,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "existential and economic importance, and \nabout why it's in danger of being lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey Everybody before we get started I wanted \nto let you know that August 8th was the 94th  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37120,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "birthday of Sir Roger Penrose. The work of Sir \nRoger and his famous Penrose diagram have been an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "important part of Space Time and to celebrate we \nhave a limited edition Penrose diagram pin. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49120,
    "dDurationMs": 3677,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pin is based off of our original design of the \nPenrose diagram that is actually featured in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52797,
    "dDurationMs": 2963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planetarium at American Museum of Natural History. \nThe pin will only be available via pre-sale  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55760,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through mid September. We’re also offering 10% off \nfor the first 24 hours as well as 5% off all our  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63320,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "penrose inspired merch. There’s links to the merch \nstore in the description. Now on to the episode."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69680,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look again at that dot. That's here. \nThat's home. That's us. In 1990,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Carl Sagan asked NASA to turn the Voyager I \nspacecraft around for one last snapshot of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its planet of origin before it began its \nlong, cold journey towards interstellar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space. The result was this image, dubbed \nthe Pale Blue Dot, and if you haven’t heard  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sagan’s full speech and want existential \nshivers, there’s a link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We normally think of astrophysics \nas an outward-looking science,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but one of the most important reasons to look \noutwards is to better understand ourselves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one of the most important reasons to \nbuild telescopes in space is to keep a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108720,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "careful eye on the most precious planet in \nthe universe—our own Earth. Historically,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of this good work has fallen to \nNASA because no one else has the same  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119200,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "level of joint expertise and experience in \nboth rocket science and planetary science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126160,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of NASA’s Earth-watching programs is the \nOrbiting Carbon Observatory; the OCO program,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is dedicated to high-sensitivity, high \nresolution observations of atmospheric carbon  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137280,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dioxide. The program stumbled at first; OCO-1 \nnever quite made it to orbit after its launch  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145200,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vehicle faring failed to separate. That was \nin 2009. OCO-2 launched successfully in 2014,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and with the spare parts from both 1 and 2 \nNASA managed to assemble a third instrument,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OCO-3, which now resides on the \nInternational Space Station. In fact,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161040,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OCO-3 wouldn’t exist if OCO-1 \nhadn’t failed, so, silver lining?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166880,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From now on, if I’m referring to both OCO-2 \nand 3 I’ll say OCO. Despite the rocky start,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OCO is performing quite a bit \nbetter than expected. In fact,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it has a pretty remarkable ability that \nwasn’t even planned. I’ll come back to that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First the specs. OCO-2 is part of \nthe A-train—a close-flying chain of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Earth-observing satellites for cross-checks and \ncombined science. This satellite constellation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190400,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flies a near-polar, 100-ish-minute orbit at \naround 700 km. The orbit is sun-synchronous,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means the path maintains its orientation \nrelative to the Sun, and that helps with the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202800,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consistency of OCO-2’s measurements. OCO-3, being \non the ISS, has lower, faster orbit. Together,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211520,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the OCOs produce high-resolution maps \nof CO2 density across the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216960,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do they do this? When sunlight reflects \noff Earth and passes back through the atmosphere,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each type of air molecule absorbs a particular \nset of wavelengths, revealing absorption lines—a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229840,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sort of barcode—when that light is broken into \na spectrum. OCO captures the spectrum around two  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the infrared CO₂ and around one of the oxygen \nlines. The depth of the lines is sensitive to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242640,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "number of molecules while their width carries \ninformation about pressure and temperature.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The oxygen line is useful for things like \npath length and geometry. With these data,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253360,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the OCO pipeline applies sophisticated physics \nlike radiative transfer models to solve an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259920,
    "dDurationMs": 9120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inverse problem: “What CO₂ profile best explains \nthese spectra given the viewing geometry?” The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269040,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "result is a stunningly precise average density \nof CO₂ along the column of the observation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These measurements allow OCO to map CO₂ \ncolumn density with a spatial resolution  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a few kilometers and a sensitivity of \naround a part per million. This reveals the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sources and sinks of atmospheric carbon \ndown to neighbourhood-level precision.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293040,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it does this frequently enough to see \nseasonal swings and year-to-year anomalies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Combined with other atmospheric data, \nOCO’s observations are used to build  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303360,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "highly detailed models of the circulation of \nCO2 around the globe. This is important for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knowing not just where CO2 is being \nproduced, but also where it ends up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312560,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When OCO-2 launched, it executed its intended \nfunctions exactly as planned. And then it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319040,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "revealed an ability that no one expected. It \ncould literally see plants breathing—-the faint  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325760,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "glow emitted by plants during photosynthesis. \nWhen chlorophyll is energized by incoming light,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most goes to fueling the plant, but some \nof that energy is quickly reemitted as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337760,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infrared light. Sunlight that is simply \nreflected off the Earth’s surface retains  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the dark absorption lines of the incoming \nsunlight. But this photosynthetic glow  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349440,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "partially fills in those bands, allowing OCO \nto measure the “solar induced fluorescence”.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this way we can now measure when and \nhow efficiently plants are breathing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362880,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has broad and incredibly powerful \napplications. Combined with other data,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369280,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OCO allows us to watch the natural daily and \nseasonal shifts in plant metabolism across  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375760,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the globe. It also allows us to monitor the \nhealth of critical photosynthesizing systems,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from forests to savannas to \nocean algae to agriculture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386080,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, OCO facilitates the prediction \nand assessment of oncoming droughts in a way  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that was previously impossible. A plant’s \nphotosynthesis efficiency drops very quickly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396880,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in response to stress, for example due to the \nheat and dryness that precedes a drought. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403040,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these changes happen before there’s any visible \nchange in the plantlife. Because OCO can monitor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photosynthesis, it can track how vegetation \nis responding to harsh conditions. In fact,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414400,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it’s the response of vegetation often \nworsens and even causes the drought;  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as temperatures rise before the drought, \nplants actually become more productive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in the process draw water down into \nthe ground. When temperatures then spike,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "soil moisture has become dangerously low, \nleading to the onset of flash drought in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436160,
    "dDurationMs": 8560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mere days. SIF monitoring is our best tool for \ncatching this dangerous cycle before it happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s not just security from catastrophic \nfailure. OCO also enables us to perform  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450320,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "highly nuanced measurements of plant metabolism, \nwhich lets us assess stress, forecast growth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and generally do global vegetation health \nmonitoring. Arguably the most important  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461360,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "application of this is in crop yields. OCO’s SIF \ndata has been used to predict US corn-belt crop  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468160,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yields down to the county level. It can do this \nwith better accuracy than current USDA methods,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and much sooner. It’s hard to \noverstate the importance of this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Besides the obvious fact that we have a \nlot of people to feed, agriculture is an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enormous part of the economy. In the US, \nagriculture and its dependent industries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "represent several hundred billion to 1.5 \ntrillion dollars in economic activity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494000,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depending on how you count, and employ 10s of \nmillions of people. More reliable crop yield  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prediction is ultimately important for \neveryone, and this benefit is very much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505280,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weighted to rural communities. And farmers \nin particular. For example, they often rely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510640,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on futures contracts—payments based on crop yield \npredictions—to finance their efforts. Better yield  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517520,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predictions means better financial security \nfor farmers and food security for everyone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A primary goal of the OCO program was to track \nCO₂ for the purpose of climate change modeling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530080,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and mitigation. However, the program is way \nbroader than this and would be a no-brainer even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537520,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without the climate factor. OCO can pinpoint \ncarbon sources and plant metabolic activity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543920,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which can be a powerful strategic tool, both \nfor geopolitical and humanitarian reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, it enables us to keep \ntrack of carbon-intensive activity like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "urban or industrial development, whether of \nfriends or rivals, with remarkable resolution.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560160,
    "dDurationMs": 9360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It could literally see a single new powerplant \nor large factory, no matter how well hidden. It  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can also monitor changes in global crop \nhealth, enabling the prediction of crop  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "failure and the potential resulting famines \nand refugee crises. Regardless of what you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think we should do about such things, \nit’s always better to know in advance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584960,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And heaven forbid a major conflict breaks out \nbetween world powers … but if that happens it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seems prudent to retain the ability to sense \nnew industrial buildup, shifts in land use,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supply chains, etc; efforts that might \notherwise be screened from direct observation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600400,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s amazing that we have this capability. \nCurrently both OCO-2 and 3 are in perfect  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "working order and could run well into the 2030s \nand further. They were a big investment to build,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at around 750 million, however the \nongoing cost is relatively cheap,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a combined budget of 16.4 \nmillion proposed for this year—a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny fraction of the potential returns \nfor their benefit to agriculture alone,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626880,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to say nothing of the much larger risk-cost \nanalysis against existential concerns like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633760,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "environmental and food security, and even defence \nconcerns. Let me reiterate, no nation other than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641440,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US nor private organization has anything \napproaching the capabilities of the OCO program."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649920,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nonetheless, OCO was zeroed out in the White \nHouse’s budget request for NASA this year,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657360,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2025. NASA’s OCO team has been directed to plan \nfor a mission close-out. That means switching off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664560,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OCO-3 and de-orbiting OCO-2—burning it up in the \natmosphere. This still needs to be approved by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Congress, so it’s not a done deal. But there’s a \nfair chance that all of these amazing capabilities  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675920,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you just learned about will literally go up in \nflames. It’s not too late, but it will be soon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, it IS possible to build and launch new \nfacilities. There was a plan to build GeoCarb - a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687280,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "satellite with similar sensitivities to sit in \ngeostationary over the Americas. It would have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693760,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been a great complement to OCO because it would \nincrease resolution in NASA’s home continent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699680,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while OCO continues its global surveillance. \nThe project was canceled due to cost overruns,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705440,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so currently there are no plans for new \nOCO-like facilities. If we ever do replace OCO,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we’d be much, much better off replacing \nit while it’s still running. OCO now has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717520,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a decade-long baseline of global monitoring. \nShutting that down means breaking a continuous  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time series that future satellites \nwill need for cross-calibration and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728240,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continuity. From a data analysis perspective, \nthat cross-calibration is incredibly important,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734240,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to say nothing of the importance of \ncontinuity from a security perspective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753360,
    "dDurationMs": 9360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sagan usually said it best. Our planet is a lonely \nspeck in the great enveloping cosmic dark. In our  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obscurity, in all this vastness, there is no hint \nthat help will come from elsewhere to save us from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767680,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ourselves. NASA’s oft-stated prime directive \nis to explore the unknown in air and space,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "innovate for the benefit of humanity, and \ninspire the world through discovery. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "image of the Earth as a lonely blue speck, barely \na pixel across, surrounded by the vast emptiness  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784640,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of space certainly does that. So does OCO’s \nexquisitely resolved surveillance of a living,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790880,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "breathing planetary biosphere, our only known \nrefuge in a vast and inhospitable spacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to DeleteMe for supporting PBS. \nDeleteMe helps protect you from more than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "800 data brokers. Data brokers are companies \nthat scrape public records, mine social media,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and buy commercial data to build and sell detailed \nprofiles, often without individuals ever knowing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does it work? Well platform searches through \nhundreds of data broker sites, identifies where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820400,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your information is exposed, and issues official \nremoval requests. But they don’t just remove your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826480,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "information once—DeleteMe keeps monitoring, so \nif a site tries to slip your details back online,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they’ll work to remove it again. You’ll also \nget regular Privacy Reports showing exactly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where your info was found and removed, plus \na dashboard for business customers to track  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "progress across their teams. With a family plan, \nthese protections extend to linked household  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849920,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "members—reducing the chance brokers can map your \nconnections. Get 20% off any DeleteMe consumer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856640,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or family plan at joindeleteme.com/spacetime with \npromo code spacetime. Link’s in the description."
    } ]
  } ]
}
